# Optimization
#
# A method matrix for linear programs, convex problems, gradient methods, dynamic programming, and optimal control, with the duality that prices every constraint.

#>mathematics_optimization
#:layer #!reference
#:domain #!mathematics
#:form #!comparison
#:level #!advanced
#:review #!adversarial_checked
#:valence #!boon

^"emit"{
 ~#title: "Optimization"
 ~#claim: "Every constrained optimum carries a price for each constraint, and convexity is what makes a local answer global and those prices sufficient."
 ~#proof: "Kantorovich and Dantzig founded linear programming; Karush, Kuhn, and Tucker gave the conditions; Boyd and Vandenberghe state the convex theory."
 ~#door: "Solve the bakery problem by hand, then read duality, then follow the bridge to revenue management."
 ~#audience: "engineering, operations, and economics students after multivariable calculus"
 continuity: "Optimization | price for each constraint"
 cold_open: "Every constrained optimum carries a price for each constraint, and that price tells you what one more unit is worth."
}

